# 詞: 銀包

1. 我今日出街唔記得帶銀包，連搭車都冇錢。 (I forgot to bring my wallet when I went out today, so I didn't even have money for the bus.)
2. 佢個銀包好靚，係佢阿媽送畀佢嘅生日禮物。 (His wallet is very beautiful; it was a birthday gift from his mother.)
3. 唔好將銀包放喺後褲袋，好容易畀人偷。 (Don't put your wallet in your back pocket; it's easy for someone to steal it.)
4. 我個銀包唔見咗，入面有身份證同信用卡，要即刻報警。 (My wallet is missing; it had my ID card and credit cards inside, so I need to report it to the police immediately.)
5. 佢成日都話自己冇錢，但係個銀包就成日都好鼓。 (He always says he has no money, but his wallet is always bulging.)
6. 呢個銀包係真皮造嘅，用咗幾年都仲好新。 (This wallet is made of genuine leather; it still looks new after several years of use.)
7. 買嘢之前記得睇清楚銀包入面仲有幾多現金。 (Before buying things, remember to check how much cash is left in your wallet.)
8. 佢喺地鐵站執到一個銀包，即刻交畀職員。 (He found a wallet at the MTR station and immediately handed it to the staff.)
9. 我個銀包太細，連八達通同身份證都放唔落。 (My wallet is too small; it can't even fit my Octopus card and ID card.)
10. 送銀包畀人做禮物，有「財源滾滾」嘅意思。 (Giving a wallet as a gift symbolizes "rolling in wealth" or continuous prosperity.) [end of text]


